      "grouping_at_time": "Design and Construction",
      "title_at_revision": "Flight crew emergency exits.",
      "text": "Except for airplanes with a passenger capacity of 20 or less in which the proximity of passenger emergency exits to the flight crew area offers a convenient and readily accessible means of evacuation for the flight crew, the following apply:\n(a) There must be either one exit on each side of the airplane or a top hatch, in the flight crew area.\n(b) Each exit must be of sufficient size and must be located so as to allow rapid evacuation of the crew. An exit size and shape of other than at least 19 by 20 inches unobstructed rectangular opening may be used only if exit utility is satisfactorily shown, by a typical flight crewmember, to the Administrator.",
